1:1 COMMENT "# range_forms.z -- the forms of an integer range in a `for` header."
1:68 EOL "\n"
2:1 COMMENT "#"
2:2 EOL "\n"
3:1 COMMENT "# `each` is the COUNT form: `N.each` walks [0, N) and hands back an ordinary"
3:77 EOL "\n"
4:1 COMMENT "# iterator, so a header drives it and a binding does too. `iterate` is the"
4:75 EOL "\n"
5:1 COMMENT "# older stepper, which takes a `from:` and is not an iterator at all."
5:70 EOL "\n"
6:1 COMMENT "#"
6:2 EOL "\n"
7:1 COMMENT "# Both must reach the counted-loop path: the step emitter accepted either by"
7:77 EOL "\n"
8:1 COMMENT "# interned id while the bound reader compared the spelling \"iterate\" alone, so"
8:79 EOL "\n"
9:1 COMMENT "# `for x: N.each loop` fell through to the iterator protocol, never advanced,"
9:78 EOL "\n"
10:1 COMMENT "# and printed the receiver forever."
10:36 EOL "\n"
11:1 EOL "\n"
